{"name":"Willow Brook","hex":"#dfe6cf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"willow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various deciduous trees or shrubs in the genus Salix, in the willow family Salicaceae, found primarily on moist soils in cooler zones in the northern hemisphere.","The wood of these trees."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To open and cleanse (cotton, flax, wool, etc.) by means of a willow.","To form a shape or move in a way similar to the long, slender branches of a willow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/willow"},{"term":"brook","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bear; endure; put up with; tolerate.","To enjoy the use of; make use of; profit by; to use, enjoy, possess, or hold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A body of running water smaller than a river; a small stream.","A water meadow, or  low, marshy ground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brook"}],"entries":[{"title":"Willow Brook (Otsego Lake tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Willow Brook is a river in Otsego County, New York. It drains out of Moe Pond, flows through Cooperstown, and empties into Otsego Lake."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Brook_(Otsego_Lake_tributary)","wikidata":"Q30628713"},{"title":"Willow Brook (River Nene)","blocks":[{"text":"The Willow Brook is a tributary of the River Nene. Its entire course is in the English county of Northamptonshire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Willow_Brook_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1258704.jpg/330px-Willow_Brook_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1258704.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Brook_(River_Nene)","wikidata":"Q8022271"},{"title":"Willow Brook (Utley Brook tributary)","blocks":[{"text":"Willow Brook is a tributary of Utley Brook in Susquehanna County and Wyoming County, in Pennsylvania, in the United States. It is approximately 3.7 miles (6.0 km) long and flows through Lenox Township in Susquehanna County and Nicholson Township in Wyoming County. The surficial geology in the vicinity of the stream consists mainly of Wisconsinan Till, bedrock, alluvium, wetlands, and a lake. A number of bridges have been constructed across it. The stream is classified as a Coldwater Fishery and a Migratory Fishery."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Brook_(Utley_Brook_tributary)","wikidata":"Q27989242"},{"title":"Willow","blocks":[{"text":"Willows, also called sallows and osiers, of the genus Salix, comprise around 350 species of typically deciduous trees and shrubs. They are primarily found on moist soils in cold and temperate regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Salix_alba_Morton.jpg/330px-Salix_alba_Morton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow","wikidata":"Q36050"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg/500px-Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg/500px-Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"At the base of the petiole, a pair of stipules form. These may fall in spring, or last for much of the summer or even for more than one year (marcescence).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalix_silesiaca_a5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Young-catkin.jpg/500px-Young-catkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Young-catkin.jpg/500px-Young-catkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young male catkin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoung-catkin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg/500px-Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg/1280px-Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg/500px-Bourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pollard willow and woodpile in the Bourgoyen-Ossemeersen, Ghent, Belgium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABourgoyen_knotted_willow_and_woodpile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kopfweiden_1.jpg/500px-Kopfweiden_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kopfweiden_1.jpg/1280px-Kopfweiden_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Kopfweiden_1.jpg/500px-Kopfweiden_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Berlin Britzer Garten pollarded willow tree in the spring of March 2018","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKopfweiden_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Weeping_Willow_by_Pond.jpg/500px-Weeping_Willow_by_Pond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Weeping_Willow_by_Pond.jpg/500px-Weeping_Willow_by_Pond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Weeping willow, an example of a hy